    values:originalText "(1) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, make a Code setting out conditions that are to be complied with in relation to consultations under clause 29.  (2) The Code may specify the manner and form in which a consultation is to occur.  (3) Subclause (2) does not, by implication, limit subclause (1).  (4) A carrier must comply with the Code.  (5) This clause does not, by implication, limit a power conferred by or under this Act to make an instrument.  (6) This clause does not, by implication, limit the matters that may be dealt with by codes or standards referred to in Part 6.  (7) Subclauses (5) and (6) do not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3B) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  Standard carrier licence conditions  Schedule 1 Access to telecommunications transmission towers and to underground facilities  Part 5  Clause 30  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
