concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-1-sec-34-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "34(2) Access to sites of telecommunications transmission towers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-34-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The first carrier is not required to comply with subclause (1) unless:  (a) the access is provided for the sole purpose of enabling the second carrier to install a facility used, or for use, in connection with the supply of a carriage service by means of radiocommunications; and  (b) the second carrier gives the first carrier reasonable notice that the second carrier requires the access." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The first carrier is not required to comply with subclause (1) unless:  (a) the access is provided for the sole purpose of enabling the second carrier to install a facility used, or for use, in connection with the supply of a carriage service by means of radiocommunications; and  (b) the second carrier gives the first carrier reasonable notice that the second carrier requires the access."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eec6e0aa30320f12a39180018a49d4231b791c2642577edac95d53f167b80fe6" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-1-sec-34 ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Access to sites of telecommunications transmission towers is permitted for the sole purpose of enabling a second carrier to install a facility used in connection with the supply of a carriage service by means of radiocommunications, subject to reasonable notice." ;
