doc:sch-1-sec-34-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "34(3) Access to sites of telecommunications transmission towers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The first carrier is not required to comply with subclause (1) in relation to a particular site if there is in force a written certificate issued by the ACCC stating that, in the ACCC’s opinion, compliance with subclause (1) in relation to that site is not technically feasible." ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-1-sec-34-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "34(4) Access to sites of telecommunications transmission towers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-34-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) In determining whether compliance with subclause (1) in relation to a site is technically feasible, the ACCC must have regard to:  (a) whether compliance is likely to result in significant difficulties of a technical or engineering nature; and  (b) whether compliance is likely to result in a significant threat to the health or safety of persons who operate, or work on, a facility situated on the site; and  (c) if compliance is likely to have a result referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)—whether there are practicable means of avoiding such a result, including (but not limited to):  (i) changing the configuration or operating parameters of a facility situated on the site; and  (ii) making alterations to a facility situated on the site; and  (d) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant." ;
    skos:definition "(4) In determining whether compliance with subclause (1) in relation to a site is technically feasible, the ACCC must have regard to:  (a) whether compliance is likely to result in significant difficulties of a technical or engineering nature; and  (b) whether compliance is likely to result in a significant threat to the health or safety of persons who operate, or work on, a facility situated on the site; and  (c) if compliance is likely to have a result referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)—whether there are practicable means of avoiding such a result, including (but not limited to):  (i) changing the configuration or operating parameters of a facility situated on the site; and  (ii) making alterations to a facility situated on the site; and  (d) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b3b17da14318b34456bea7d08d2bfce1dd4d16746a2ac648729739387d445f3f" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-1-sec-34 ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The ACCC must consider certain factors when determining technical feasibility of compliance." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.30" ;
