doc:sch-1-sec-45 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45 Definitions" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: active declared service means:  (a) an active declared service within the meaning of section 152AR of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or  (b) a declared service (within the meaning of subsection 152AL(8A) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010) that an NBN corporation supplies (whether to itself or to other persons); or  (c) a declared service within the meaning of subsection 152AL(8D) or (8E) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010. Note: Subsections 152AL(8A), (8D) and (8E) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 deal with services supplied by an NBN corporation. designated interconnection service has the meaning given by clause 47. eligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010.  Standard carrier licence conditions  Schedule 1 Any-to-any connectivity  Part 7  Clause 46  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-1-sec-46 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "46 Carriers must obtain designated interconnection services from"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-46 ;
    values:originalText "carriage service providers for the purpose of ensuring any-to-any connectivity  (1) If:  (a) a carrier owns, or supplies a carriage service over, a telecommunications network (the carrier’s telecommunications network); and  (b) a carriage service provider supplies a carriage service over a telecommunications network (the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network); and  (c) any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network is interconnected with the carrier’s telecommunications network;  (ii) the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network is to be interconnected with the carrier’s telecommunications network;  (iii) the carriage service provider is seeking to have the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network interconnected with the carrier’s telecommunications network; and  (d) the carriage service provider requests the carrier to obtain from the carriage service provider a designated interconnection service for the purpose of ensuring that each end-user who is:  (i) connected to the carrier’s telecommunications network; and  (ii) supplied with a carriage service that involves communication between end-users;  is able to communicate, by means of that carriage service, with an end-user who is connected to the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network; the carrier must obtain the designated interconnection service from the carriage service provider.  Schedule 1  Standard carrier licence conditions" ;
    skos:definition "carriage service providers for the purpose of ensuring any-to-any connectivity  (1) If:  (a) a carrier owns, or supplies a carriage service over, a telecommunications network (the carrier’s telecommunications network); and  (b) a carriage service provider supplies a carriage service over a telecommunications network (the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network); and  (c) any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network is interconnected with the carrier’s telecommunications network;  (ii) the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network is to be interconnected with the carrier’s telecommunications network;  (iii) the carriage service provider is seeking to have the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network interconnected with the carrier’s telecommunications network; and  (d) the carriage service provider requests the carrier to obtain from the carriage service provider a designated interconnection service for the purpose of ensuring that each end-user who is:  (i) connected to the carrier’s telecommunications network; and  (ii) supplied with a carriage service that involves communication between end-users;  is able to communicate, by means of that carriage service, with an end-user who is connected to the carriage service provider’s telecommunications network; the carrier must obtain the designated interconnection service from the carriage service provider.  Schedule 1  Standard carrier licence conditions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9d2d2e5f6ab229dfbcc2b4f9218e12f1dbe1a0da22f984ae863c4966ebf8d178" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Carrier must obtain designated interconnection services from carriage service providers." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
