concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-2-sec-13-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13(5) Itemised billing"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-13-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) For the purposes of the application of this clause to a carriage service provider who supplies a standard telephone service to a customer, a designated local call is a call that:  (a) is made using that service; and  (b) is made between points in the applicable zone in relation to the provider and in relation to the customer; and  (c) is not an exempt call (as defined by subclause (6)).  Schedule 2  Standard service provider rules" ;
    skos:definition "(5) For the purposes of the application of this clause to a carriage service provider who supplies a standard telephone service to a customer, a designated local call is a call that:  (a) is made using that service; and  (b) is made between points in the applicable zone in relation to the provider and in relation to the customer; and  (c) is not an exempt call (as defined by subclause (6)).  Schedule 2  Standard service provider rules"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "572543254f62642d55d1e393d82dc52cb494d0881c06a87da1d3130c06adc6c3" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-2-sec-13 ;
