concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-2-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Simplified outline"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • This Part deals with priority assistance for people with life-threatening medical conditions. • A carriage service provider must comply with the priority assistance industry code. • If a carriage service provider receives an inquiry from a prospective residential customer about the supply of a standard telephone service, and the provider does not offer priority assistance, the provider must:  (a) inform the prospective residential customer that the provider does not offer priority assistance in connection with the service; and  (b) inform the prospective residential customer of the names of one or more carriage service providers from whom the prospective residential customer can obtain priority assistance." ;
    skos:definition "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • This Part deals with priority assistance for people with life-threatening medical conditions. • A carriage service provider must comply with the priority assistance industry code. • If a carriage service provider receives an inquiry from a prospective residential customer about the supply of a standard telephone service, and the provider does not offer priority assistance, the provider must:  (a) inform the prospective residential customer that the provider does not offer priority assistance in connection with the service; and  (b) inform the prospective residential customer of the names of one or more carriage service providers from whom the prospective residential customer can obtain priority assistance."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f8eed0ac85d2741e5cfa35be797f9f8a37252f869e7d29891490dd98896f1b3a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must inform prospective residential customer about priority assistance" ;
    dc:description "Informing prospective residential customer" ;
