concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3-sec-37 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37 Exemption from State and Territory laws"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-37 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies to an activity carried on by a carrier if the activity is authorised by Division 2, 3 or 4.  (2) The carrier may engage in the activity despite a law of a State or Territory about:  (a) the assessment of the environmental effects of engaging in the activity; or  (b) the protection of places or items of significance to Australia’s natural or cultural heritage; or  (c) town planning; or  (d) the planning, design, siting, construction, alteration or removal of a structure; or  (e) the powers and functions of a local government body; or  (f) the use of land; or  (g) tenancy; or  (h) the supply of fuel or power, including the supply and distribution of extra-low voltage power systems; or  (i) a matter specified in the regulations.  (3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply to a law in so far as the law provides for the protection of places or items of significance to the cultural heritage of Aboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders.  Carriers’ powers and immunities  Schedule 3 General provisions  Part 1 Exemptions from State and Territory laws  Division 7  Clause 38  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) Paragraph (2)(h) does not apply to a law in so far as the law deals with the supply of electricity at a voltage that exceeds that used for ordinary commercial or domestic requirements." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause applies to an activity carried on by a carrier if the activity is authorised by Division 2, 3 or 4.  (2) The carrier may engage in the activity despite a law of a State or Territory about:  (a) the assessment of the environmental effects of engaging in the activity; or  (b) the protection of places or items of significance to Australia’s natural or cultural heritage; or  (c) town planning; or  (d) the planning, design, siting, construction, alteration or removal of a structure; or  (e) the powers and functions of a local government body; or  (f) the use of land; or  (g) tenancy; or  (h) the supply of fuel or power, including the supply and distribution of extra-low voltage power systems; or  (i) a matter specified in the regulations.  (3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply to a law in so far as the law provides for the protection of places or items of significance to the cultural heritage of Aboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders.  Carriers’ powers and immunities  Schedule 3 General provisions  Part 1 Exemptions from State and Territory laws  Division 7  Clause 38  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) Paragraph (2)(h) does not apply to a law in so far as the law deals with the supply of electricity at a voltage that exceeds that used for ordinary commercial or domestic requirements."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "311bf37a1ef85ec700a1b177ccc6d9367e8380cb71729c14614a215c50e3a5f3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "126"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3-sec-37-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3-sec-37-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3-sec-37-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3-sec-37-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.126" .
doc:sch-3-sec-37 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "37 Exemption from State and Territory laws" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies to an activity carried on by a carrier if the activity is authorised by Division 2, 3 or 4.  (2) The carrier may engage in the activity despite a law of a State or Territory about:  (a) the assessment of the environmental effects of engaging in the activity; or  (b) the protection of places or items of significance to Australia’s natural or cultural heritage; or  (c) town planning; or  (d) the planning, design, siting, construction, alteration or removal of a structure; or  (e) the powers and functions of a local government body; or  (f) the use of land; or  (g) tenancy; or  (h) the supply of fuel or power, including the supply and distribution of extra-low voltage power systems; or  (i) a matter specified in the regulations.  (3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply to a law in so far as the law provides for the protection of places or items of significance to the cultural heritage of Aboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders.  Carriers’ powers and immunities  Schedule 3 General provisions  Part 1 Exemptions from State and Territory laws  Division 7  Clause 38  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) Paragraph (2)(h) does not apply to a law in so far as the law deals with the supply of electricity at a voltage that exceeds that used for ordinary commercial or domestic requirements." ;
    cof:pageNumber "126"^^xsd:integer .

