    skos:definition "(2) In performing the function conferred on the ACMA by subclause (1), the ACMA must have regard to the following matters:  (a) if:  (i) the ACMA is satisfied that a body or association represents carriers; and  (ii) the body or association has given the ACMA a written statement setting out the body’s or association’s views about how the ACMA should perform that function;  the views set out in the statement;  (b) the legitimate business interests of carriers;  (c) the objective of safeguarding national security;  (d) the privacy of end-users of carriage services supplied by means of the lines, towers or facilities concerned."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5b9dca6168aee1ef81924261f397553e7212310ae17106cc259276e565c20801" ;
