doc:sch-3-sec-60 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "60 Existing buildings, structures and facilities—application of State" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "and Territory laws  A law of a State or Territory that relates to:  (a) the standards applicable to:  (i) the design; or  (ii) the manner of the construction;  of a building, structure or facility; or  (b) the approval of the construction of a building, structure or facility; or  (c) the occupancy, or use, of a building, structure or facility; or  (d) the alteration or demolition of a building, structure or facility; does not apply to a building, structure or facility that is owned or operated by a carrier to the extent that the construction, alteration or demolition of the building, structure or facility was or is authorised by:  (e) section 116 of the Telecommunications Act 1991; or  (f) Division 3 of Part 7 of the Telecommunications Act 1991; or  (g) a repealed law of the Commonwealth." ;
    cof:pageNumber "139"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3-sec-61 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "61 Existing buildings, structures and facilities—application of the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-61 ;
    values:originalText "common law  A rule of the common law that relates to trespass does not apply to the continued existence of a building, structure or facility that is owned or operated by a carrier to the extent that the construction or alteration of the building, structure or facility was or is authorised by:  (a) section 116 of the Telecommunications Act 1991; or  (b) Division 3 of Part 7 of the Telecommunications Act 1991; or  (c) a repealed law of the Commonwealth.  Schedule 3  Carriers’ powers and immunities" ;
    skos:definition "common law  A rule of the common law that relates to trespass does not apply to the continued existence of a building, structure or facility that is owned or operated by a carrier to the extent that the construction or alteration of the building, structure or facility was or is authorised by:  (a) section 116 of the Telecommunications Act 1991; or  (b) Division 3 of Part 7 of the Telecommunications Act 1991; or  (c) a repealed law of the Commonwealth.  Schedule 3  Carriers’ powers and immunities"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d54e0435446cc2832e0dfcc0c508d19519bc1a784b6aff6f694ed9cb6ff5577b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "139"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No common law rule applies to a carrier's building if authorized by specific laws." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
