    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If, on a trial for an offence against clause 41:  (a) the arbiter of fact is not satisfied that the defendant engaged in the activity with the intention of making a commercial gain; and  (b) the arbiter of fact is otherwise satisfied that the defendant has committed an offence against clause 40; the arbiter may find the defendant not guilty of the offence against clause 41 but guilty of an offence against clause 40, so long as the defendant has been accorded procedural fairness in relation to that finding of guilt." ;
    cof:pageNumber "171"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-44 a cml:Concept ;
