    values:originalText "or restricted activities  (1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person is the owner or master of a ship; and  (b) the first person permits another person to use the ship; and  (c) the other person commits an offence against clause 40 or 41; and  (d) the ship is used in the commission of the offence and the first person is reckless as to that fact. Penalty:  Schedule 3A  Protection of submarine cables" ;
