    values:originalText "(5) In this clause: non-compulsory refusal means a refusal to grant a protection zone installation permit, other than a refusal that is required by this clause.  Protection of submarine cables  Schedule 3A Permits to install submarine cables  Part 3 Protection zone installation permits  Division 2  Clause 58  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
