concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-71 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "71 Matters to which the ACMA must have regard in making a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3a-sec-71 ;
    values:originalText "decision about a permit  In deciding whether to grant a non-protection zone installation permit, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the objective of facilitating the supply of efficient, modern and cost-effective carriage services to the public; and  (aa) if the Secretary of the Attorney-General’s Department or the Home Affairs Secretary makes a submission to the ACMA under clause 70—that submission; and  (c) any relevant technical and economic aspects of the installation; and  (d) whether the installation involves co-location of the submarine cable or cables to which the application relates with one or more other submarine cables; and  (e) any other matters that the ACMA considers relevant." ;
    skos:definition "decision about a permit  In deciding whether to grant a non-protection zone installation permit, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the objective of facilitating the supply of efficient, modern and cost-effective carriage services to the public; and  (aa) if the Secretary of the Attorney-General’s Department or the Home Affairs Secretary makes a submission to the ACMA under clause 70—that submission; and  (c) any relevant technical and economic aspects of the installation; and  (d) whether the installation involves co-location of the submarine cable or cables to which the application relates with one or more other submarine cables; and  (e) any other matters that the ACMA considers relevant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f80ab3da7839ef1bad4524231486e2606dde0c0b9437bded230742e71f3de2e3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "195"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ACMA must consider specific factors when deciding on a permit" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
