doc:sch-3a-sec-71 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "71 Matters to which the ACMA must have regard in making a" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "decision about a permit  In deciding whether to grant a non-protection zone installation permit, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the objective of facilitating the supply of efficient, modern and cost-effective carriage services to the public; and  (aa) if the Secretary of the Attorney-General’s Department or the Home Affairs Secretary makes a submission to the ACMA under clause 70—that submission; and  (c) any relevant technical and economic aspects of the installation; and  (d) whether the installation involves co-location of the submarine cable or cables to which the application relates with one or more other submarine cables; and  (e) any other matters that the ACMA considers relevant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "195"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-72a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "72A Refusal of permit—security"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3a-sec-72a ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Home Affairs Minister, after consulting the Prime Minister and the Minister administering this Act, considers that the grant of a non-protection zone installation permit to a particular carrier would be prejudicial to security, the Home Affairs Minister may give a written direction to the ACMA not to grant a non-protection zone installation permit to the carrier.  (2) The ACMA must comply with a direction under subclause (1).  (3) While a direction is in force under this clause:  (a) the ACMA cannot reconsider a non-compulsory refusal to grant a non-protection zone installation permit to the carrier; and  Schedule 3A  Protection of submarine cables" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Home Affairs Minister, after consulting the Prime Minister and the Minister administering this Act, considers that the grant of a non-protection zone installation permit to a particular carrier would be prejudicial to security, the Home Affairs Minister may give a written direction to the ACMA not to grant a non-protection zone installation permit to the carrier.  (2) The ACMA must comply with a direction under subclause (1).  (3) While a direction is in force under this clause:  (a) the ACMA cannot reconsider a non-compulsory refusal to grant a non-protection zone installation permit to the carrier; and  Schedule 3A  Protection of submarine cables"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "081c66004a0a090b5ec209633a58f70e48da0616d6a0b4eddf4f0a122c45b91c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "195"^^xsd:integer ;
