concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "86 Failing to comply with ACMA direction to remove an unlawfully"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3a-sec-86 ;
    values:originalText "installed international submarine cable  (1) The ACMA may direct a carrier to remove an international submarine cable if:  (a) the carrier installed the submarine cable, or caused it to be installed, in a protection zone or in Australian waters without a permit under this Part authorising the installation; or  (b) the carrier is installing the submarine cable, or causing it be installed, in a protection zone or in Australian waters without a permit under this Part authorising the installation.  (2) A carrier who does not comply with a direction under subclause (1) commits an offence. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (3) The ACMA must not give a direction to a carrier under subclause (1) in relation to an international submarine cable that the carrier installed, or began to install, before the commencement of this Schedule." ;
    skos:definition "installed international submarine cable  (1) The ACMA may direct a carrier to remove an international submarine cable if:  (a) the carrier installed the submarine cable, or caused it to be installed, in a protection zone or in Australian waters without a permit under this Part authorising the installation; or  (b) the carrier is installing the submarine cable, or causing it be installed, in a protection zone or in Australian waters without a permit under this Part authorising the installation.  (2) A carrier who does not comply with a direction under subclause (1) commits an offence. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (3) The ACMA must not give a direction to a carrier under subclause (1) in relation to an international submarine cable that the carrier installed, or began to install, before the commencement of this Schedule."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "79b93f921fdda1d17a31f1338589808eac6800413305c65daf7e1cfcafdc7950" ;
    cof:pageNumber "206"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.206" .
doc:sch-3a-sec-86 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "86 Failing to comply with ACMA direction to remove an unlawfully" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "installed international submarine cable  (1) The ACMA may direct a carrier to remove an international submarine cable if:  (a) the carrier installed the submarine cable, or caused it to be installed, in a protection zone or in Australian waters without a permit under this Part authorising the installation; or  (b) the carrier is installing the submarine cable, or causing it be installed, in a protection zone or in Australian waters without a permit under this Part authorising the installation.  (2) A carrier who does not comply with a direction under subclause (1) commits an offence. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (3) The ACMA must not give a direction to a carrier under subclause (1) in relation to an international submarine cable that the carrier installed, or began to install, before the commencement of this Schedule." ;
    cof:pageNumber "206"^^xsd:integer .

