concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "86A Failing to comply with ACMA direction to remove an"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3a-sec-86a ;
    values:originalText "unlawfully installed domestic submarine cable  (1) The ACMA may direct a carrier to remove a domestic submarine cable if:  Protection of submarine cables  Schedule 3A Permits to install submarine cables  Part 3 Offences in relation to installation of submarine cables  Division 5  Clause 86A  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) the carrier installed the submarine cable, or caused it to be installed, in a protection zone without a permit under this Part authorising the installation; or  (b) the carrier is installing the submarine cable, or causing it to be installed, in a protection zone without a permit under this Part authorising the installation.  (2) A carrier who does not comply with a direction under subclause (1) commits an offence. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (3) The ACMA must not give a direction to a carrier under subclause (1) in relation to a domestic submarine cable that the carrier installed, or began to install, before the commencement of this clause.  Schedule 3A  Protection of submarine cables" ;
    skos:definition "unlawfully installed domestic submarine cable  (1) The ACMA may direct a carrier to remove a domestic submarine cable if:  Protection of submarine cables  Schedule 3A Permits to install submarine cables  Part 3 Offences in relation to installation of submarine cables  Division 5  Clause 86A  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) the carrier installed the submarine cable, or caused it to be installed, in a protection zone without a permit under this Part authorising the installation; or  (b) the carrier is installing the submarine cable, or causing it to be installed, in a protection zone without a permit under this Part authorising the installation.  (2) A carrier who does not comply with a direction under subclause (1) commits an offence. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (3) The ACMA must not give a direction to a carrier under subclause (1) in relation to a domestic submarine cable that the carrier installed, or began to install, before the commencement of this clause.  Schedule 3A  Protection of submarine cables"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "04fa8282a7e0656077477712cbc3803217f5d9dd03a78f82ec3380bd63ab8b18" ;
    cof:pageNumber "206"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-86a-ss-2 ;
