concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sch-3a-sec-90 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "90 Delegation by the Home Affairs Secretary"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3a-sec-90 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Home Affairs Secretary may, by writing, delegate any or all of his or her powers under this Schedule to an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Home Affairs Department.  (2) A delegate must comply with any directions of the Home Affairs Secretary.  Reviewable decisions of the ACMA  Schedule 4 Decisions that may be subject to reconsideration by the ACMA  Part 1  Clause 1  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Home Affairs Secretary may, by writing, delegate any or all of his or her powers under this Schedule to an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Home Affairs Department.  (2) A delegate must comply with any directions of the Home Affairs Secretary.  Reviewable decisions of the ACMA  Schedule 4 Decisions that may be subject to reconsideration by the ACMA  Part 1  Clause 1  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
